{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton"}],"externalID":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton.swift#L29"},"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","roleHeading":"Structure"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Tries\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the trie of the patterns with two more links per state: the failure link, to the state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the longest proper suffix of the state’s prefix that is also a prefix of some pattern, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the output link, to the nearest state along the failure links at which a pattern ends. A scan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the trie while the text matches and the failure links where it stops matching, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads each symbol of the text once and reports all the matches in O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}]},{"text":") for a text of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"text":" symbols with ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}]},{"text":" matches.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","for match in automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\") {","    print(match.patternIndex, match.range)","}","\/\/ 1 1..<4   (\"she\")","\/\/ 0 2..<4   (\"he\")","\/\/ 3 2..<6   (\"hers\")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Matches come in order of where they end, and of those ending at one place, longest first.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Ranges count the text’s symbols from 0. The automaton is built once and is immutable.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Symbols are mapped to dense indices at construction, through a 256-entry table when they are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a dictionary otherwise, so a scan over bytes, such as a string’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"utf8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", does no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hashing. When the states times the distinct symbols are few enough, every transition is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precomputed into a table, and a scan takes one load per symbol.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/Match","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/MatchesView","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct"],"generated":true},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/init(patterns:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/stateCount","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/containsMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/firstMatch(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/matches(in:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(at:)","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/patternLength(checkedAt:)"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"},"abstract":[{"text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975).","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","